---
import LabAssessment from "../../components/LabAssessment.astro";
import { MAL_ENTENDIDOS_DO_INCIDENTE } from "@ovh/otel-domain";
import { IncidenteModos } from "../../components/IncidenteModos.tsx";
import { Predicao } from "../../components/Predicao.tsx";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteNav from "../../components/SiteNav.astro";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { url } from "../../lib/urls";
import "../../styles/docs.css";
import "../../components/ModosDoLab.css";
import "../../components/CpuVitrine.css";
import "../../components/ContextoLab.css";
import "../../components/ImplantacaoLab.css";
import "../../components/MetricaLab.css";
import "@ovh/motion/src/react/motion.css";
import "@ovh/stage3d/src/iso.css";
import "../../components/Predicao.css";
---

<Base
  domain="otel"
  title="The cost of disconnected signals — OpenLabs"
  description="An error log with only a timestamp points at every request active in that second — dozens at ordinary traffic, more as load grows. A trace_id on the same line points at one. The difference is the time it takes to find the cause."
>
  <SiteNav current="labs" />

  <main id="content">
    <section class="lab-head editorial">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lab-head__eyebrow mono">
          <a href={url("handbooks/otel")}>OpenTelemetry Visual Handbook</a> · lab
        </p>
        <h1>A timestamp is not a link</h1>
        <p>
          The alert fires. The error line says <code>12:00:02 payment
          declined</code>. You have traces, and you have logs — and the only
          thing they share is the clock. In that second, thirty-two requests
          were running. One of them is the one you want.
        </p>
        <p>
          Joining by time feels good enough until you count. The number of
          candidates is the number of requests in flight, so it grows with
          traffic and not with how bad the error is. A <code>trace_id</code> on
          the log line makes it one, at any load.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="lab-head__note mono">
        <p>The MTTR clock is a model.</p>
        <p>Its assumptions are on screen; use your own numbers.</p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="lab-palco">
      <IncidenteModos client:only="react" />
    </section>

    <section class="lab-prosa editorial">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Break it</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <b>Search by time at 20 req/s.</b> Count the candidates the second
            returns, and read the clock.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>Go to 80 req/s.</b> Same error, same second — several times the
            candidates and the minutes.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>Turn on trace_id on the log line.</b> One candidate, at any
            traffic. The cost stops depending on load.
          </li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Predict before you look</h2>
        <p>Answer first, then try it in the simulation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lab-predicao">
        <Predicao
          client:visible
          pergunta="A service handles 80 requests a second, each lasting up to a second. An error log has a timestamp to the second and no trace_id. Roughly how many traces could it belong to?"
          opcoes={[
            "Around a hundred — every request active in that second",
            "One — the log was written by exactly one request",
            "Around eighty — the requests that started in that second",
          ]}
          correta={0}
          revelacao="Requests overlap. The candidates are all requests running at any moment in that second: those that started in it, plus those still running from the second before. At 80 req/s with durations up to a second, that is over a hundred. Only an identifier carried by both the log and the trace narrows it to one."
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="lab-prosa editorial">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What people get wrong</h2>
        <p>Each row is a belief the simulation is built to take apart. The right column is the specification, with the link.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lab-mal-entendidos">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">What people believe</th>
              <th scope="col">What the spec says</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              MAL_ENTENDIDOS_DO_INCIDENTE.map((m) => (
                <tr>
                  <td>{m.crenca}</td>
                  <td>
                    {m.spec}{" "}
                    <a href={m.fonte} rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">
                      source
                    </a>
                  </td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="lab-prosa editorial">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Where this connects</h2>
        <p>
          <a href={url("labs/three-pillars")}>Three pillars</a> is the same blind
          spot on one incident; this lab is what it costs as traffic grows.
          <a href={url("labs/hard-context-and-baggage")}>Hard context and
          baggage</a> is how the id gets there, and
          <a href={url("labs/a-log-that-knows-its-trace")}>A log that knows its
          trace</a> is how it gets onto the log line.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <LabAssessment href="labs/disconnected-signals" />
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .lab-head {
    padding-block: var(--space-4) var(--space-2);
  }

  .lab-head__eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-1);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: var(--size-step--1);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--size-step-2);
    max-width: 24ch;
  }

  .lab-head__note {
    align-self: end;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--size-step--1);
  }

  .lab-head__note p {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
  }

  .lab-palco {
    margin-block: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
  }

  .lab-prosa {
    padding-block-end: var(--space-4);
  }

  .lab-predicao {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .lab-mal-entendidos {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .lab-mal-entendidos table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    font-size: var(--size-step--1);
  }

  .lab-mal-entendidos th,
  .lab-mal-entendidos td {
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-2);
    text-align: start;
    vertical-align: top;
  }
</style>
